</nav>

<main id="main-content">
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero__container">
      <div class="hero__content">
        <p class="hero__label">GOTS Certified | Full Supply Chain | Since 1998</p>
        <h1 class="hero__title">GOTS Certified Clothing Manufacturer | Organic Cotton Supply Chain Certification Since 1998</h1>
        <p class="hero__description">
          SDF Clothing is a GOTS certified clothing manufacturer providing full supply chain organic cotton certification. We provide transaction certificates for every production batch, ensuring traceability from organic farm to finished garment. We serve EU, UK, and US brands with verified GOTS production since 1998. Get certified organic clothing manufacturing with full documentation.
        </p>
        <div class="hero__stats">
          <div class="hero__stat">
            <span class="hero__stat-value">1998</span>
            <span class="hero__stat-label">Founded</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero__stat">
            <span class="hero__stat-value">GOTS</span>
            <span class="hero__stat-label">Certified</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero__stat">
            <span class="hero__stat-value">TC</span>
            <span class="hero__stat-label">Provided</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero__stat">
            <span class="hero__stat-value">95%+</span>
            <span class="hero__stat-label">Organic</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__ctas">
          <a href={whatsappQuoteUrl} class="hero__cta hero__cta--primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Get GOTS Manufacturing Quote
          </a>
          <a href="/certifications" class="hero__cta hero__cta--secondary">
            View GOTS Certificate
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__image">
        <img src="/factory.webp" alt="SDF Clothing GOTS certified organic cotton manufacturing facility with full supply chain certification" width="600" height="400" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Trust Indicators -->
  <section class="trust">
    <div class="trust__container">
      <div class="trust__items">
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">GOTS Certified</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">Transaction Certificates</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">Full Supply Chain</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">Organic Cotton</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">No Toxic Chemicals</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">Fair Labor Certified</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 1: What is GOTS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">What is GOTS Certification for Clothing?</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard) is the worldwide leading textile processing standard for organic fibers, including ecological and social criteria. GOTS certification covers the entire textile supply chain from harvesting of raw materials through environmentally and socially responsible manufacturing to labeling. GOTS ensures organic status of textiles from harvesting of raw materials through environmentally and socially responsible manufacturing to labeling, providing credible assurance to the consumer.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        GOTS was developed by leading standard setters with the aim of defining worldwide recognized requirements for organic textiles. The standard covers the processing, manufacturing, packaging, labeling, trading, and distribution of all textiles made from at least 70% certified organic natural fibers. GOTS certification requires independent third-party certification of the entire supply chain, from fiber producers to textile manufacturers to traders and retailers. This comprehensive scope ensures that organic claims are substantiated at every stage of production.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        GOTS certification includes both environmental and social criteria. Environmental criteria prohibit the use of toxic heavy metals, formaldehyde, aromatic solvents, and genetically modified organisms. Requirements cover wastewater treatment, packaging materials, and environmental management systems. Social criteria are based on International Labour Organization conventions and cover fair wages, working conditions, no forced or child labor, freedom of association, and discrimination prohibition. GOTS is unique in combining organic and ethical standards in one certification.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">GOTS Certification Scope</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        This table outlines the scope of GOTS certification, what each stage covers, and the verification requirements. GOTS certification applies to the entire supply chain from fiber to finished garment.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <table style="width:100%;max-width:1000px;border-collapse:collapse;background:#0a0a0a;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="background:#e00;">
              <th style="padding:1rem;text-align:left;color:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #333;">Supply Chain Stage</th>
              <th style="padding:1rem;text-align:left;color:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #333;">GOTS Requirements</th>
              <th style="padding:1rem;text-align:left;color:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #333;">Verification</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Fiber Production</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Organic farming, no GMOs, no toxic pesticides</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Organic certification (EU, USDA, etc.)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Yarn & Fabric</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Restricted chemicals, wastewater treatment</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">GOTS certification, TCs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Garment Manufacturing</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Restricted inputs, social compliance</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">GOTS certification, TCs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Trading & Distribution</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Traceability, segregation of organic</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">GOTS certification, TCs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Labeling</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Accurate grade claims, GOTS logo use</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">GOTS certification, license</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      
      <p class="section__text" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <em>Table: GOTS certification scope across supply chain stages. Each stage requires independent certification. Source: Global Organic Textile Standard version 7.0.</em>
      </p>

      <p class="section__text">
        SDF Clothing holds GOTS certification for garment manufacturing with full supply chain traceability. We provide transaction certificates for every production batch, proving the organic status of materials from fiber to finished garment. Our <a href="/organic-cotton-clothing-manufacturer/">organic cotton manufacturing</a> services include complete GOTS documentation and verification support. Our <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-bangladesh">Bangladesh operations</a> and <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-vietnam/">Vietnam operations</a> both hold GOTS certification. For brands requiring GOTS certification for EU or US market access, we provide the documentation needed for regulatory compliance.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Transaction Certificates -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">GOTS Transaction Certificates | Traceability from Farm to Garment</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        GOTS transaction certificates (TCs) are the backbone of organic textile traceability. A TC is a document proving the organic status of materials at each stage of the supply chain, from fiber to finished garment. TCs trace organic materials through every processing step, ensuring no conventional cotton is mixed in and that organic integrity is maintained throughout production. Every GOTS certified manufacturer must provide TCs for each production batch, making TCs essential for substantiating organic claims.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Transaction certificates include detailed information about the organic materials used, including fiber type, weight, certification status, and origin. TCs track materials as they move through ginning, spinning, knitting/weaving, dyeing, and garment manufacturing. Each transfer between certified entities requires a new TC, creating a complete chain of custody. Brands receive TCs for their orders, enabling them to prove the organic status of their products to retailers, regulators, and consumers.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Many retailers and regulators require TCs as proof of organic status. EU organic regulations and USDA organic labeling rules both require transaction certificates for organic textile claims. Major retailers including department stores and ethical fashion retailers demand TCs before accepting organic products. Without TCs, organic claims cannot be substantiated and may violate consumer protection laws. GOTS certified manufacturers must provide TCs for every production batch - this is a non-negotiable requirement of certification.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Transaction Certificate Information</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        This table shows the key information included in a GOTS transaction certificate and why each element matters for traceability and verification.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <table style="width:100%;max-width:1000px;border-collapse:collapse;background:#0a0a0a;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="background:#e00;">
              <th style="padding:1rem;text-align:left;color:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #333;">TC Element</th>
              <th style="padding:1rem;text-align:left;color:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #333;">Information Provided</th>
              <th style="padding:1rem;text-align:left;color:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #333;">Why It Matters</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Certificate Number</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Unique TC identifier</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Verification through GOTS database</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Fiber Type & Weight</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Organic fiber content and quantities</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Organic percentage verification</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Certification Status</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">GOTS grade (organic or made with organic)</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Label claim accuracy</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Supplier & Recipient</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Certified entities in the transaction</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Chain of custody tracking</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Batch Reference</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Production batch identification</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Traceability to specific production</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      
      <p class="section__text" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <em>Table: GOTS transaction certificate elements and their importance for traceability. TCs are required for every production batch. Source: GOTS certification requirements.</em>
      </p>

      <p class="section__text">
        SDF Clothing provides transaction certificates for every GOTS production batch. TCs are issued within 7 days of production completion and include all information needed for retailer and regulatory verification. Our <a href="/certifications">certifications page</a> includes instructions for verifying TCs through the GOTS database. For brands requiring TCs for specific retailer compliance, we provide additional documentation as needed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: GOTS Label Grades -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">GOTS Label Grades | Organic vs Made with Organic</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        GOTS has two label grades with different organic fiber requirements: 'organic' requires minimum 95% certified organic fibers, while 'made with organic' requires minimum 70% certified organic fibers. Both grades prohibit toxic chemicals, require wastewater treatment, mandate fair labor practices, and require third-party certification. The choice between grades depends on product requirements, market positioning, and cost considerations.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        The 'organic' label (grade 1) allows only 5% non-organic fibers, and these must be for specific technical reasons such as elastane in stretch fabrics or recycled fibers. This grade carries the strongest organic claim and is preferred for premium positioning. The 'made with organic' label (grade 2) allows up to 30% non-organic fibers, providing more flexibility for blended fabrics or functional requirements. Both grades provide credible organic certification, but the 'organic' grade commands higher consumer recognition and premium pricing.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Labeling requirements differ between grades. The 'organic' grade allows use of the GOTS logo with 'organic' text, while the 'made with organic' grade allows the GOTS logo with 'made with organic' text. Both grades require the GOTS certification number to be displayed. Brands must ensure label claims match the TC certification grade - mislabeling is a violation of GOTS certification and may result in certification withdrawal and legal penalties.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">GOTS Label Grade Comparison</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        This table compares the two GOTS label grades, their requirements, and appropriate use cases. Choose the grade that matches your product requirements and market positioning.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <table style="width:100%;max-width:1000px;border-collapse:collapse;background:#0a0a0a;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="background:#e00;">
              <th style="padding:1rem;text-align:left;color:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #333;">Requirement</th>
              <th style="padding:1rem;text-align:left;color:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #333;">Organic (Grade 1)</th>
              <th style="padding:1rem;text-align:left;color:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #333;">Made with Organic (Grade 2)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Organic Fiber Minimum</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">95% certified organic fibers</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">70% certified organic fibers</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Non-Organic Fiber Allowance</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Maximum 5% for technical reasons only</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Maximum 30%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Label Claim</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">'Organic' with GOTS logo</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">'Made with organic' with GOTS logo</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;">
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Consumer Recognition</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Higher recognition, premium positioning</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Moderate recognition, flexible positioning</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;">Best For</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Pure organic products, premium segments</td>
              <td style="padding:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:0.82rem;">Blended fabrics, functional requirements</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      
      <p class="section__text" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <em>Table: GOTS label grade comparison showing requirements and use cases. Both grades require full GOTS certification. Source: GOTS labeling requirements version 7.0.</em>
      </p>

      <p class="section__text">
        SDF Clothing produces both GOTS grade levels based on client requirements. For brands seeking the strongest organic claim, we recommend the 'organic' grade with 95%+ organic fibers. For brands requiring functional blends or cost optimization, the 'made with organic' grade provides flexibility while maintaining credible organic certification. Our <a href="/insights/gots-label-guide">GOTS labeling guide</a> provides detailed instructions for compliant labeling across both grades.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: How to Verify GOTS -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">How to Verify GOTS Certification</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Verifying GOTS certification is essential because certificates can be forged and unsubstantiated organic claims violate consumer protection laws. The verification process involves checking the certificate number through the official GOTS database, validating transaction certificates for your specific production, and ensuring the manufacturer holds current certification. Verification protects your brand from greenwashing accusations and ensures your organic claims are legally defensible.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Start by requesting the GOTS certificate number from your manufacturer. Visit the official GOTS database at global-standard.org and search for the certificate number. The database will show the certification status, validity dates, and scope of certification. Check that the certificate is current and that the factory name matches the certificate holder. Expired certificates or name mismatches indicate potential issues that require further investigation.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Beyond certificate verification, request transaction certificates for your specific production batch. TCs prove that the materials used in your order were certified organic through the supply chain. Check that the TC certificate number matches your production batch and that the organic percentage matches your order specifications. Genuine GOTS manufacturers provide TCs willingly - refusal to provide TCs is a red flag indicating potential certification issues.
      </p>

