      <h2 class="section__title">GOTS Certified Manufacturing Costs | Is Organic More Expensive?</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Yes, GOTS certified organic cotton manufacturing costs more than conventional production, but the premium enables significant retail price increases. GOTS production typically costs 10-15% more than conventional cotton due to organic fiber premiums, restricted chemical inputs, wastewater treatment requirements, and certification costs. However, GOTS certified products command 20-40% retail price premiums as consumers pay significantly more for verified organic products.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Organic cotton fiber costs 20-30% more than conventional cotton due to lower yields and certification requirements. GOTS restricted chemical inputs increase processing costs as certified organic dyes and auxiliaries cost more than conventional alternatives. Wastewater treatment requirements add capital and operational costs for proper effluent management. Certification costs including annual audits, documentation systems, and transaction certificate issuance add 1-3% to production costs. When combined, these elements typically total 10-15% above conventional cotton manufacturing.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        However, GOTS certification enables substantial retail price premiums. Consumer research shows that 70-80% of consumers are willing to pay more for organic clothing, with actual premiums ranging from 20-40% for GOTS certified products. This premium more than covers the 10-15% production cost increase, making GOTS manufacturing highly profitable when properly positioned and marketed to organic-conscious consumers. Additionally, GOTS certification provides regulatory compliance benefits and protects against greenwashing accusations.
